# Local evidence corpus (never commit images)
corpus/

# Case directories written by `omnitrace analyze --out DIR`. The directory
# name is the examiner's choice -- AKGM007, case-router, info35l -- so no
# pattern catches every one. These catch the manifest and listing files
# wherever they land, and `cases/` is the suggested place to keep them.
#
# This is a guard against the accident, not a guarantee: a case also holds
# carved partitions and an extracted tree that these patterns do not name.
# scripts/check_docs.py fails the build if case output is ever tracked.
cases/
**/filesystems/*/files/
**/containers/*/files/
**/.omnitrace-versions/
**/symbols/
**/INFO.yaml
**/manifest.yaml
**/listing.yaml
**/SOURCE.yaml
**/report.html
**/report.md
**/INFO.md
**/summary.md
**/partitions.md
**/platform.yaml
**/platform.md
**/artifacts.yaml
**/artifacts.md
**/certificates.yaml
**/certificates.md
**/mount.sh

# Raw evidence and anything carved out of it. This repository has never
# tracked a disk image and never should: the fixtures are generated
# (tests/fixtures/out, ignored above) and the corpus is local. A deliberate
# addition still works with `git add -f`, which check_docs.py then catches.
*.bin
*.BIN
*.img
*.dd
*.raw
